[Music]  one of gamescom's biggest trailers this  year was for an upcoming game title doe  kv  the trailer was fun stylish and flashy  and had pokemon in a big city vibes but  ultimately we still don't know all that  much about the game  so what the heck is doke v and why am i  so excited about a trailer that  ultimately didn't really show that much  gameplay to start doke v is being made  by pearl abyss this is a south korean  game developer whose credits consist of  black desert a sandbox mmorpg black  desert mobile the mobile version of this  and shadow arena a battle royale game  that was originally a mini game from  black desert pearl abyss actually has a  game scheduled to release by the end of  the year crimson desert which is an  action adventure rpg  and  so far that's it pearl abyss is a  relatively new company and dokey v is  completely different in style and tone  to their previous games according to  their announcement in 2019 dokey v was  originally said to be an mmo game  similar to black desert over development  this has changed and it's now a creature  collecting open world action adventure  according to the official website  they have stated there will be a  narrative focus to the game around  collecting dokey b so i have to imagine  this game will be somewhat similar to  final fantasy xv or assassin's creed and  how open the world will be but add in  pokemon style collecting and a more  action rpg oriented combat system  as seen in the trailer the game will  have strong creature collecting elements  where you'll be collecting dokey b  i'm sure it's no coincidence that this  sounds incredibly similar to the  legendary creatures from korean  mythology known as  doka bee or korean goblins in korean  folklore doke b are powerful spirits  that typically formed out of the  possession of inanimate objects they  also usually appear in dark creepy  corners at night or on a foggy rainy day  similar to many mythological beings do  kb can range from being kind to cruel  and are often mischievous they have  immense abilities and some are believed  to cause fires and disease while others  are helpful and can bring good fortune  and wealth and crops  all of that said i'm sure the dokeby of  korean mythology served as a very light  inspiration for the creatures of the  game  similar to the yokai of yokai watch  watching the trailer one of the things  that immediately stood out to me was all  of the different forms of travel that  you can use i spotted bicycling  skateboarding longboarding floating and  mid-air hopping via umbrella bouncy  balls llamas rollerblading rocket shoes  spider-man style webs that form in  mid-air jet skiing and mini cars and  while no one was actually on one as  someone who loves surfing drop in just  smack the lip  i really really hope surfing is a part  of the game as there was a brief scene  of characters by the beach with a bunch  of boards it's hard to tell as of yet  how much these modes of transportation  will truly make a difference for the  overall gameplay but it does make the  city seem like a playground the trailer  showed off various tricks the player  could do on many of these modes of  transportation and as the game is open  world in style maybe that means racking  up combos and tricks will actually be  some sort of mini game either way it  definitely looks like it will be a blast  to travel around  the actual gameplay itself shown  consisted of two elements the first of  these was an action game where it looks  like the pack on your character's back  can be used to pull out all sorts of  weapons for different kinds of attacks  these look to be creative toys that are  enhanced in size like a giant toy hammer  or a bouncy ball that can be used to  smash enemies we also saw water guns and  arrows meaning that you'll have a mix of  melee and ranged attacks all of the  actions shown included your character  needing to run and dodge from enemies  while it's unclear as of yet if there  will be rpg mechanics to the game the  combat itself definitely looks like a  fun take on the action genre according  to the team the action combat was  originally inspired by their own  previous games so taking a look at black  desert and the upcoming crimson desert  might be good indicators as to how the  game will play the other element we saw  comes from creature collecting unlike  pokemon and other similar turn-based  creature collecting rpgs in doke v  you'll actually be fighting alongside  the creatures you collect many of these  dokey b look like they not only have  unique attacks of their own but also  unique ways you can partner up with them  to strike against your foes it  definitely adds to the depth of the  combat and makes the game look even  stronger in my opinion  you may be unaware but the game's first  trailer was actually released in 2019  this particular trailer features the  character fighting off enemies with a  whole team of dokeby and there's brief  glimpses of the same thing in the newest  trailer which means that you'll be able  to assemble a whole fighting roster of  your dokey b and hopefully they'll have  unique cooperative attacks not only with  you as the player but with each other's  as well meaning you'd be able to put  together synergistic combinations if  that's the case  as far as how you collect these dokey b  i'm still not entirely sure there are  quests you activate to collect these  dokey b where you'll have to meet a  certain requirement first to me it  sounds similar to an rpg where you have  to own a special weapon and be level 20  then talking to the correct npc will  activate a quest to collect a special  weapon  except in this game it would be dokey b  according to the developers and i quote  as you progress through the story you  will meet and collect numerous dokeby  you will be able to activate the events  related to adokeb when you fulfill  special requirements then you can  collect the doki b as you progress  through a unique story hints related to  dokeby can be found not only in towns  but across the world discovering the  hints to encounter more doki b will also  be a fun aspect of the game  during this specific scene in the  trailer we see the character bust out a  vacuum and seemingly defeat an enemy in  a special way  if i were to guess this is actually the  character collecting another dokey b  so if that's the case the game will be  similar to pokemon in that you'll be  able to collect your monsters after  fighting them and weakening them  considering ghostbusters was one of the  influences on the game this does seem  pretty likely  although  that said considering the dokeb of  folklore come from inanimate objects who  knows maybe you actually find the dokey  b by exploring and finding the right  item as given to you within a quest  some other minor things are we see the  player's character at one point using  magic to change outfits it's not a big  thing but that along with all of the  other clothes in the game does showcase  that you'll be able to change your  clothes and likely collect new outfits  throughout the game the first trailer  showed a brief tease of a scuba diving  element so unless that was taken out of  the final product hopefully that means  you'll be able to explore underwater as  well  many aspects of korean culture were also  included in the game to give the game a  sense of familiarity as it drew from  real culture the beginning of the  trailer including my favorite brief  surfboard scene also shows your  character interacting with other normal  people this includes other kids playing  at a playground and someone fishing so  there will be some level of interaction  with people but how much is completely  unknown thus far  according to the lead producer this game  is about the main character going out to  collect okb with her friends the team  set out to make a family-friendly game  with the kids of the game actually  acting like kids they also wanted to  include comedy and fun interactions for  the player  personally a lot of the game reminded me  of when i first saw pokemon as a kid and  immediately connected with me hopefully  doke v will be as good as it looks as we  really haven't seen too much of how the  game will truly play  currently there's no release dates set  for doke v and it's set to come to pc  and console but which consoles are  unclear  are you looking forward to doke v or  cautiously optimistic about it let us  know in the comments below and hopefully  this shapes out to be something truly  special  [Applause]  [Music]  hello  [Music]

